  "published": "2025-07-19T18:03:53.71Z",
  "readmeFile": "getting-started-guide-20.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## **Release Notes - ASCDataAccessLibrary v2.0**\n\n**Major Release: Tag-Based Blob Indexing and Lambda Expression Support**\n\nThis release adds **tag-based indexing for Azure Blob Storage** with up to 10 searchable tags per blob for fast queries, **lambda expression support** for both Table and Blob storage operations, and **hybrid filtering** that automatically optimizes between server-side and client-side processing. The AzureBlobs class now operates on a single container and includes lambda-based bulk operations for downloads and deletes. Key improvements include 10-100x faster blob searches using tags, simplified upload methods with automatic naming, and enhanced file type management. **Breaking changes**: AzureBlobs constructor now requires container name, and some method signatures have been simplified. Lambda expressions work with both storage types: `dataAccess.GetCollectionAsync(x => x.Status == \"Active\")` for tables and `blobs.GetCollectionAsync(b => b.Tags[\"type\"] == \"invoice\")` for blobs. The library now provides enterprise-grade performance with modern C# syntax while maintaining full async/await support.",
  "repository": "",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "ASC Azure Table Storage Data Access Library",
